  "body": "What is owed:\nRotary Contour refuses a face selection by name (the fix for #2848). It cannot keep its rings to the picked faces. Rotary Parallel can.\n\nExpected:\nRotary Contour accepts picked faces of the turned surface. The rings cut only over the picked faces. The axis fit still reads the full model.\n\nWhat is known:\n- The clip is available: `crates/motion/src/multiaxis/rotary_pick.rs` keeps a cut point where the radial through the ball centre meets a picked facet. It works in a frame whose local x is the axis. The contour plans in a frame whose local z is the axis.\n- The links are the open work. Rotary Parallel links the kept pieces with `rotary_links::radial_relink`. The contour has no such relink. Its waterline certifies the plunge column of each ring entry (`finishing3d/rings.rs`). A kept piece of a ring needs an entry that is certified too.\n- The contour has no clearance radius. Its heights are stations along the axis. A radial retract needs a radius that clears the work.\n\nDone means:\n- Rotary Contour with `SrcRef::Selection` of faces cuts only over the picked faces.\n- Each link between two kept pieces is certified clear of the part, or the operation refuses by name.\n- The refusals of `operation::rotary_picks` (not a face, two models, a face that does not look away from the axis, separate groups) apply to Rotary Contour.\n- The `not_yet(\"Rotary Contour\")` refusal is removed.\n- Tests pin the kept cut, the links and the refusals.\n\nFound during the work on #2848.\n",
